D1: Service metrics that exist
fetch metric.series, from:-2h
| filter startsWith(metric.key, "dt.service")
| summarize series = count(), by:{metric.key}
| sort metric.key asc


What we're checking: the request count, failure and response-time metric names, and the unit of response time.

D2: Process and JVM metrics that exist
fetch metric.series, from:-2h
| filter startsWith(metric.key, "dt.process")
      or startsWith(metric.key, "dt.runtime")
| summarize series = count(), by:{metric.key}
| sort metric.key asc


What we're checking: whether there's a process availability metric, and which heap and GC metrics exist (and how many series each has).

D3: Which technologies Claims services run on
fetch dt.entity.service
| fields id, tags, serviceType
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize services = countDistinctExact(id), apps = countDistinctExact(apmid), by:{serviceType}
| sort services desc


What we're checking: how many Claims services are web/request services and how many are database services, and whether JVM tiles would cover enough apps to be worth building.

D4: Service and process problem types in Davis (last 30 days)
fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-30d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter contains(toString(affected_entity_types), "service")
      or contains(toString(affected_entity_types), "process")
| summarize problems = count(), by:{event.name, event.category}
| sort problems desc
| limit 30
